{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי יקח איש", :translit "ki yikach ish", :gloss "when a man takes"} {:he "לא שיוקח", :translit "lo sheyukach", :gloss "that she should not be taken"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כי יקח איש", :b "לא שיוקח"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "בה ערות דבר", :translit "ervat davar", :gloss "ervah of a matter"} {:he "בעד שאין דבר שבערוה אלא בעדים", :translit "be'ad she'ein davar shebe'ervah ela be'edim", :gloss "on behalf of — there is no matter of ervah except by witnesses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "בעד שאין דבר שבערוה אלא בעדים", :spells "בעד"}], :frame {:text "The phrase ערות דבר in Deuteronomy 24:1 is interpreted in the Mishnah as a matter of ervah, meaning unseemly conduct that justifies divorce. The school of Shammai restricts it to a matter of ervah, while the school of Hillel allow divorce for any matter (Mishnah Gittin 9:10). The question of whether actual witnesses are required for the suspected ervah is addressed in the Talmudic discussion of this verse (Ketubot 72b, Gittin 90a).", :sources ["Mishnah Gittin 9:10" "Ketubot 72b" "Gittin 90a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "דבר וכתב", :translit "davar uchtav", :gloss "matter and writing"} {:he "צריך דבור עם הכתב", :translit "tzarich dibbur im hachtav", :gloss "speech is required with the writing"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Deriving from the word דבר that verbal instruction to the scribe accompanies the written get."}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah states that a get requires the instruction (לשמה) of the husband: 'She is my wife... and this is my get' (Mishnah Gittin 7:3). The Talmud discusses whether the husband must verbally instruct the scribe or whether amicable cooperation suffices, concluding that he must say 'write for her' (Gittin 72b).", :sources ["Mishnah Gittin 7:3" "Gittin 72b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וכתב לה", :translit "ukhtav lah", :gloss "and he writes for her"} {:he "לשמה", :translit "lishmah", :gloss "for her sake"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Lishmah requirement for the get is read from the word לה — 'for her,' meaning written for her specific sake."}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah derives the requirement לשמה from the phrase וכתב לה: the get must be written for the sake of this specific woman (Mishnah Gittin 2:3, 3:1). The Talmud understands this from the word לה, meaning the writing must be directed to this particular woman (Gittin 24b, 27a).", :sources ["Mishnah Gittin 2:3" "Mishnah Gittin 3:1" "Gittin 24b" "Gittin 27a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ספר כריתת", :translit "sefer keritut", :gloss "scroll of cutting off"} {:he "ספר כריתת אמכם", :translit "sefer keritut imechem", :gloss "scroll of cutting off of your mother"} {:he "ספר כורתה ואין דבר אחר כורתה", :translit "sefer koreteh ve'ein davar acher koreteh", :gloss "the scroll cuts off and nothing else cuts off"} {:he "אשה נקנית בג' דרכים", :translit "ishah nikneit bishlosh derachim", :gloss "a woman is acquired in three ways"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ספר כריתת" "ספר כריתת" "ספר כריתת"]} {:kind :other, :note "The three occurrences map to the three modes of kiddushin; only the sefer severs."}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah states that a woman is acquired (נקנית) in three ways: money, document, or relations, and acquires her freedom (נפקא) through a get or the death of the husband (Mishnah Kiddushin 1:1). The midrashic reading on the word כריתת — 'the scroll cuts off and nothing else cuts off' — is cited by Rashi on this verse, tracing to the Talmudic principle that only a get severs the marriage bond (Gittin 85b, Kiddushin 1:1).", :sources ["Mishnah Kiddushin 1:1" "Gittin 85b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "כי יקח איש", :a-value 459, :b "לא שיוקח", :b-value 455, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "בעד שאין דבר שבערוה אלא בעדים", :spells "בעד", :letters ["ב" "ש" "ד" "ש" "א" "ב"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :other, :note "Deriving from the word דבר that verbal instruction to the scribe accompanies the written get.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Lishmah requirement for the get is read from the word לה — 'for her,' meaning written for her specific sake.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ספר כריתת" "ספר כריתת" "ספר כריתת"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ספר כריתת", :refs ["Deuteronomy 24:1" "Deuteronomy 24:3"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ספר כריתת", :refs ["Deuteronomy 24:1" "Deuteronomy 24:3"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ספר כריתת", :refs ["Deuteronomy 24:1" "Deuteronomy 24:3"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "The three occurrences map to the three modes of kiddushin; only the sefer severs.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:04.358505145Z", :model "glm-5.2"}